>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Is real estate a good career in India? Yes for some routes, and no for the one most people picture: solo commission work that pays only when a deal closes.</strong>
    Real estate is a sector with many jobs. Marketing, property management, valuation and your own registered brokerage can grow past your own hours. A lone agent depends on the next closing.
    The people who do well check the RERA rules first, stay honest with papers and cash, and build a <strong>high-value skill portfolio</strong> of selling, proof and trust. Those are the decisions that unlock high income opportunities and an earlier path to financial freedom.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Real estate is a dozen different careers. Commission-only agent work is lumpy: a month can bring a fee, or nothing. Routes with repeat income or a licensed skill (property management, valuation, marketing, your own brokerage) scale better.</li>
      <li><strong>Lead with the routes that scale, and treat solo agent work and salaried developer sales as places to learn, not places to stay.</strong></li>
      <li>You need RERA registration to facilitate sales in registered projects. Breaking the rules can cost Rs 10,000 a day, up to 5% of the cost. Maharashtra also needs training, an exam and a certificate.</li>
      <li>Next step: pick one route from the table, build a ten-property verified sheet for one small area, then talk to three people who do the work.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    This guide sits inside our <a href="/blog/career-options/">career option guides</a>. Real estate is the most sales-heavy career we cover, so if selling itself is the question, read
    <a href="/blog/career-options/is-sales-a-good-career/">is sales a good career</a> first. If you like the building side more than the selling side, the
    <a href="/blog/career-options/is-civil-engineering-a-good-career-in-india/">civil engineering career guide</a> covers site, planning and project roles.
  </p>

