  <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer to "is real estate a good career"</h2>

  <p>
    "Real estate" is not one job. A person who arranges rentals, a developer's sales executive, a registered valuer and a co-living owner all say they work in real estate. Their pay, risk and growth have little in common.
  </p>

  <p>
    The honest answer splits in two. Entry is easy. Staying paid is hard. Anyone can register and start calling, so the field is crowded, and the second filter is trust: who will a stranger hand a large sum of money to?
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Most posts on this topic show the one big fee. Few show the months in between. Judge the career by the typical month, by what your state asks you to register, and by whether you are willing to stay clean on cash and papers for many years.
    </p>
  </div>

