  </p>

  <h2 id="trust-risk">Fraud, fake listings and cash deals</h2>

  <p>
    This is the part nobody puts in the recruiting video. A broker handles large sums and strangers' trust. The same field also attracts fraud, and a broker who passes on a fake listing can lose the client, the licence and the reputation.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Recent cases and warnings</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Hyderabad police filed a report in January 2026 on pre-launch offer fraud. A Square Yards article describing it puts losses at about Rs 3,000 crore across about 2,500 victims, with 19 cases charge-sheeted.</li>
      <li>In early November 2025 Mumbai cyber police warned that fake landlords and agents post listings on OLX, Facebook Marketplace and WhatsApp groups and demand an advance by UPI to "block" the property.</li>
      <li>In August 2025 a Hyderabad owner lost Rs 12,75,711 after a caller posing as an NSG commando offered an advance rent, as reported by PTI. Owners who advertise online are targets too.</li>
      <li>Other frauds named by Square Yards: General Power of Attorney misuse, and one unit sold to several people.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      If you are cheated or see a fraud, call the National Cyber Crime Helpline 1930, use cybercrime.gov.in, or file a complaint at your local police station.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Red flags</div>
      <ul>
        {scamCompare.gold.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
